Subject: [PATCH 1/3] claude/skills/process-email: Find the oldest message with
 just
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: uurromsroxqyvmsqlkpwnnqzpnnrzskn

Which inbox message is next was decided by a notmuch query written out
in the skill. Anything else that walks the inbox, such as a driver that
runs one pass per message, would have to repeat that query and could
drift from it, so two callers might disagree on which message to take.

A get-oldest-inbox-message recipe keeps the query in one place, and the
skill asks it.
---
change-id: uurromsroxqyvmsqlkpwnnqzpnnrzskn

 .claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md | 6 ++++--
 Justfile                              | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
index f51a0f0..a457799 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
+++ b/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
@@ -93,8 +93,10 @@ rebase alone would leave it behind on an old list.
 
 ## 2. Pick the oldest inbox message
 
-    id="$(notmuch search --sort=oldest-first --output=messages \
-        --limit=1 tag:inbox)"
+`just get-oldest-inbox-message` names it. Ask it rather than querying
+notmuch yourself, so every caller agrees on which message is next:
+
+    id="$(just -f ~/lab/default.jj/Justfile get-oldest-inbox-message)"
     thread="$(notmuch search --output=threads "${id}")"
     msgid="${id#id:}"      # the bare Message-ID, for headers
 
diff --git a/Justfile b/Justfile
index a7ef001..15e3bef 100644
--- a/Justfile
+++ b/Justfile
@@ -64,3 +64,6 @@ jj-authorme revset:
 claude-mail-purge:
   NOTMUCH_CONFIG=$(realpath .notmuch-config) notmuch search --output=files 'tag:deleted' | xargs rm
 
+# print the oldest message in the lab-devel inbox, if any
+@get-oldest-inbox-message:
+  notmuch search --sort=oldest-first --output=messages --limit=1 tag:inbox
